  "body": "What happens: the \"Clippy on the touched crates\" step of `pr-test.yml` fails on the self-hosted runner for any PR that touches `camcraft-geometry`, with three `needless_range_loop` errors (\"loop variable `slot` is only used to index `e.facets`\") in `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature.rs` at lines 481, 1205 and 1486. The lines are not part of the PR that hit it.\n\nEvidence:\n- Run 43546645706 (PR 1576, head `e7d78efe`, runner `uma`): clippy step red with the three errors above. The log's help links point at `rust-1.100.0`.\n- Main at `c00ba18a9`, local Windows machine, rustc 1.99.0 / clippy 0.1.99: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` exits 0 with no lints.\n- So the runner's newer clippy (1.100) fires a lint the local 1.99 does not. No toolchain file pins the version, so runner and contributors can differ.\n\nNot verified: that the three lines are byte-identical on main and on PR 1576's head (the PR's reviewer read them as untouched by the PR).\n\nExpected: the same clippy verdict on the runner and locally, and a green clippy step for a PR that did not touch the flagged lines.\n\nSuggested fix (either or both):\n- Rewrite the three loops as iterator loops (`for (slot, f) in e.facets.iter().enumerate()` or the form clippy suggests), with no behaviour change. This is geometry code, so the change is read with care and the feature suites run.\n- Decide whether the toolchain is pinned (a `rust-toolchain.toml` is a file `pr-test.yml` refuses in a PR diff, so that part is the maintainer's decision).\n\nDone means: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean on clippy 1.100 and 1.99, and the clippy step of a `pr-test.yml` run on a geometry-touching PR is green.\n",
